{"content":[{"c":["TASKMASTER*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["An overseer of public workers who enforced their performance. Taskmasters are depicted on Egyptian bas-reliefs with whips in their hands to enforce discipline (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.1.11","r":"Exod.1.11","rawR":"Exod.1.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.1.11","value":"Exod.1.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 1:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.3.7","r":"Exod.3.7","rawR":"Exod.3.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.3.7","value":"Exod.3.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.5.6-14","r":"Exod.5.6-14","rawR":"Exod.5.6-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.5.6-14","value":"Exod.5.6-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:6-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.3.18","r":"Job.3.18","rawR":"Job.3.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.3.18","value":"Job.3.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 3:18"},"). The Hebrew verb means “to oppress.” David and Solomon had such officers. Adoram was in charge of forced labor (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.20.24","r":"2Sam.20.24","rawR":"2Sam.20.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.20.24","value":"2Sam.20.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 20:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.6","r":"1Kgs.4.6","rawR":"1Kgs.4.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.6","value":"1Kgs.4.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.12.18","r":"1Kgs.12.18","rawR":"1Kgs.12.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.12.18","value":"1Kgs.12.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.10.18","r":"2Chr.10.18","rawR":"2Chr.10.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.10.18","value":"2Chr.10.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 10:18"},"). The excesses of these men were a factor in the revolt of the northern tribes after the death of Solomon (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.12.3-14","r":"1Kgs.12.3-14","rawR":"1Kgs.12.3-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.12.3-14","value":"1Kgs.12.3-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 12:3-14"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Taskmaster","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 1:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.1.11","rawQueryValue":"Exod.1.11","sourceRefExact":"Exod.1.11"},{"anchorText":"3:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.3.7","rawQueryValue":"Exod.3.7","sourceRefExact":"Exod.3.7"},{"anchorText":"5:6-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.5.6-14","rawQueryValue":"Exod.5.6-14","sourceRefExact":"Exod.5.6-14"},{"anchorText":"Jb 3:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.3.18","rawQueryValue":"Job.3.18","sourceRefExact":"Job.3.18"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 20:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.20.24","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.20.24","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.20.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.6","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.6","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.6"},{"anchorText":"12:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.12.18","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.12.18","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.12.18"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 10:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.10.18","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.10.18","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.10.18"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 12:3-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.12.3-14","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.12.3-14","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.12.3-14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"823b0881759b951ed82566b96f482cb9cae389f17cf39d5f916616b2eeee044f","sourceItemName":"Taskmaster","sourceItemOrder":62,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Taskmaster","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Taskmaster*","title":"Taskmaster*","ver